an assumed. What is left is a bracket of two transports, and the model is entirely in the bracket. THE TWO ARE NOT THE SAME KIND OF COUPLING: `T_{vac}` carries the near body's shortfall per unit of its mass, which SATURATES because a body deeper than a mean free path shadows itself, and `T_{met}` does not. That difference is the whole of what separates a body felt as its face from one felt as its bulk", lst("\\bar{m} = " %+% text_of(Expr$show(puts$to)) %+% "", "\\bar{m}' = " %+% text_of(Expr$show(open$to)) %+% "", "g_{N} = " %+% text_of(Expr$show(gN)) %+% "")), Inferences$step("F_{g} in bodies and transport", law, via, lst((mine)("g_{N} in bodies and transport")), "and what is felt is that, enhanced by the mismatch measured against the acceleration it produces - which is why `g` stands on both sides and why the bracket names the recursion rather than printing a second `g`", lst("F_{g} = " %+% text_of(Expr$show(law)) %+% "")), Inferences$step("g_{N} at D = 3 in bodies and transport", Expr$mul(lst((front)(3), (carried_at)(3))), via, lst((mine)("g_{N} in bodies and transport")), "the arrival between two bodies in three dimensions: their two masses over the square of what separates them, times what the medium carries between them", lst("g_{N} = " %+% text_of(Expr$show(gN)) %+% "", "D = 3")), Inferences$step("F_{g} at D = 3 as one equation", Expr$mul(lst((front)(3), (carried_at)(3), enhanced)), via, lst((mine)("g_{N} at D = 3 in bodies and transport")), "and what is felt: Newton's two masses over the square of the separation, times a bracket of two transports, times the mismatch measured against the acceleration it produces. EVERY PART OF THE MODEL IS IN THE BRACKET - the front is a count of the places three-dimensional space has at a distance, and nothing was fitted to make it an inverse square", lst("F_{g} = " %+% text_of(Expr$show(law)) %+% "", "D = 3")), Inferences$step("T_{vac} at D = 3", Expr$deep_factored(Expr$evaluate(Tvac, at3)), via, lst((mine)("T_{vac}")), "the screened transport in three dimensions", lst("T_{vac} = " %+% text_of(Expr$show(Tvac)) %+% "", "D = 3")), Inferences$step("T_{met} at D = 3", Expr$deep_factored(Expr$evaluate(Tmet, at3)), via, lst((mine)("T_{met}")), "the exchange transport in three dimensions", lst("T_{met} = " %+% text_of(Expr$show(Tmet)) %+% "", "D = 3"))))
      NULL
    }))
    NULL
  })
